The bug was caused by the incorrect masking of the Program Counter (PC) lower bits when performing exception returns from ARM mode to Thumb mode. Specifically, the change in the `store_reg()` function that masked both bits 0 and 1 of the PC value caused issues in scenarios where the new CPSR indicated a transition to Thumb mode. The exception return code paths that were supposed to correctly handle the alignment for the new instruction set state were disrupted, leading to crashes and unpredictable behavior in userspace applications using Thumb instructions.
